    <section class="section">
      <h2>What is $XRP</h2>
      <p>$XRP is a digital asset used to move value across the XRP Ledger.</p>
      <p>It acts as a <span class="highlight">bridge asset</span> between currencies, systems, and pools of liquidity, allowing value to move quickly and with low cost.</p>
      <p>At its core, $XRP is a <span class="highlight">payment rail</span>.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Usage Is Everything</h2>
      <p>$XRP does not move on opinions, memes, or price fantasies. It moves on <span class="highlight">usage</span>.</p>
      <p>Usage means value actually moving across the ledger. Payments. Transfers. Liquidity. Settlement. Real transaction activity.</p>
      <p>More usage creates more demand. Less usage reduces demand.</p>
      <p>No usage means no sustained reason for long-term price strength.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>How It Actually Moves</h2>
      <p>$XRP does not move in one straight vertical line that stays there forever.</p>
      <p>It tends to move in <span class="highlight">steps</span>.</p>
      <p>Usage expands. Price moves up. Sellers take profit. Price pulls back. More usage builds. The next step forms.</p>
      <p>That cycle repeats.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
      <h2>Price Reality</h2>
      <p>We are not here to give you fantasy numbers.</p>
      <p>A $10,000 $XRP would imply a financial world operating at massive scale on the same rail, with deep liquidity, broad alignment, and continuous real usage across systems.</p>
      <p>That is not an overnight move. That is not a six month event. That is a long-term infrastructure outcome, if it ever happens at all.</p>
      <p>Thinking in instant moonshots teaches people the wrong lesson and makes them blind to what actually matters.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="section">
